[Opening "Center Game: Berger Variation"]

{Center Game: Berger Variation. Theory ends about here. From this point the game is decided by understanding rather than memory.}
1. e4 e5 2. d4 exd4 3. Qxd4 Nc6 4. Qe3 Nf6 5. Bc4 Bb4+ {Both sides have what they wanted from the opening. The middlegame will be about the centre.} 6. c3 Ba5 7. Nf3 O-O 8. O-O ! Re8 {A long think. Both continuations are playable; this one keeps more pieces on, which suits the attacker.} (8... Bxc3 Nbd2 Bxb2 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. Qd3 Nxe4 10. Qd5 Re7 11. Ng5 Qe8 ?! 12. Nxe4 Rxe4 13. Bd3 Re5 14. Qf3 Re6 15. Qg3 Ne5 16. Bf5 Rf6 17. Bc2 Bb6 18. Be3 d6 19. Nd2 Bxe3 20. Qxe3 Re6 21. Qg3 Nd7 22. Ba4 Qe7 23. h3 Nc5 24. Bc2 Re2 25. Rad1 Bd7 26. b4 Ba4 27. Bb3 Nxb3 28. axb3 Bd7 29. Nc4 Bb5 30. Na3 Bd7 31. Nc4 Re4 32. Ne3 Bc6 33. Nf5 Qe5 34. Qxe5 Rxe5 35. Nd4 Bd7 36. c4 a6 37. f3 h5 38. Rd2 Rae8 39. Kf2 h4 40. Rc1 g5 41. b5 a5 42. Ne2 b6 43. f4 Rf5 44. Rc3 f6 45. Rd4 Rc5 46. Rcd3 Bc8 47. Nc3 Bb7 48. g3 hxg3+ 49. Rxg3 Kf7 50. Ne2 Rh8 51. fxg5 fxg5 52. Ke1 Rf5 53. Kd2 Kf6 54. Rdd3 Rh4 55. Rg1 a4 56. bxa4 Rxc4 57. Rd4 Rxd4+ 58. Nxd4 Rf2+ 59. Kc3 Bg2 60. Re1 Bxh3 61. Re8 Kf7 62. Ra8 g4 63. Rh8 Bg2 64. Rh7+ Kf6 65. Rxc7 Be4 66. Kb4 g3 67. Rc3 g2 68. Rg3 Rb2+ 69. Kc3 Ra2 70. Rg4 Rxa4 71. Ne2 d5 72. Kb2 Rb4+ 73. Kc1 Rb1+ 74. Kd2 Rxb5 75. Rg8 Rb1 76. Ng3 g1=Q 77. Nxe4+ dxe4 78. Rxg1 Rxg1 79. Ke3 Rd1 80. Kf4 b5 81. Kg4 b4 82. Kh4 Rd3 83. Kh5 Kf5 84. Kh4 b3 85. Kh5 {The endgame is winning but not simple — the passed pawn needs its king, not just its rook.} Rh3# 0-1

