[Opening "Sicilian Defense: Taimanov Variation, Bastrikov Variation, English Attack"]

{Sicilian Defense: Taimanov Variation, Bastrikov Variation, English Attack. Book so far. The plan is the usual one: finish development, then decide which side to open.}
1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nc6 5. Nc3 Qc7 {A slight inaccuracy in move order — the bishop is better placed before this pawn commits.} 6. Be3 a6 7. Qf3 Nf6 8. O-O-O ! Ne5 {The critical moment. The pieces are as good as they are going to get; something has to happen now.} (8... a5 Kb1 a4 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. Qg3 b5 10. f4 Neg4 11. Bg1 h5 ?! 12. e5 b4 13. Na4 Nd5 14. h3 Nh6 15. f5 Bb7 16. Bd3 Be7 17. Kb1 h4 18. Qe1 Nf4 19. Nb6 Rd8 20. Nc4 Nxd3 21. cxd3 Bd5 22. Rc1 Bxc4 23. Rxc4 Qa5 24. fxe6 fxe6 25. Bf2 Qd5 26. Qe3 O-O 27. Nf3 b3 28. axb3 Rb8 29. d4 Rb6 30. Rhc1 {Precise to the end. A pawn move here instead would have let the defence build a fortress.} Nf5 1/2-1/2

